<title>USA: SEC acts against Texas firm for CMO sales to towns.</title>
<headline>SEC acts against Texas firm for CMO sales to towns.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The SEC said on Thursday it launched an administrative proceedings against five former employees of a Houston government securities firm for the sale of risky mortgage derivatives to municipalities and colleges.</p>
<p>The Securities and Exchange Commission said that Aubrey O'Connor, Rick Pierson, James Winter, Gregory Bowen and Kenneth Ward sold or supervised the sale of highly sensitive collateralized mortgage obligations (CMOs) while employees of GSC, formerly Government Securities Corporation of Texas.</p>
</text>
